id=a52sxq_resolution_systemui_misc
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: SystemUI pixel constants follow Display > Screen resolution
author=kusti420
description=UNTESTED-ON-DEVICE. Static findings of the resaudit (surfaces that cannot be automated: front-camera protection ring, power-key screen-off reveal, edge lighting). (1) camera_protection_stroke_width = 37px is read raw and cached: the black ring round the punch hole while a front camera is open is 1.15 mm at FHD+, 1.72 mm at HD+, 2.30 mm at 540p; written in mm (patches/resolution_scaling scales the physical dpi) and re-read per cutout view. (2) LightRevealScrimRepositoryImpl computes the power-key reveal centre (975 px x current/native width) once in its constructor, so after a live switch the screen-off/on reveal is centred 30 mm (HD+) / 60 mm (540p) too low until SystemUI restarts; PowerButtonReveal now derives it from the current scrim size. (3) Edge lighting DrawEdgeLayout only knows the factors 4/3 and 2/3 for a non-1080 short side; at 540p the corner radius came out 104 instead of 78 native px; the factor is now short side / 1080.
